<h1>Gary Gygax presents <em>Lejendary Adventure</em> &trade;</h1>
<p class="in">Lejendary Adventure is a multi-genre roleplaying game that is easy 
for the beginner to learn, yet complex enough to keep even the most experienced gamer satisfied. The game is 
skill based, allowing for maximum character diversity and creativity. Gamers accustom to class based systems 
will thrive in the system using the many established Orders. Straight forward base mechanics allow play to 
proceeds quickly, with a focus on role-playing rather than rules referencing.</p>
<p class="in">Exlore this site to learn more about the latest roleplaying game from the creator of Dungeons &amp; 
Dragons &trade; the game that started it all. <a href="template.php?page=purchase&amp;style=blaze" 
title="support this site and buy lejendary adventure">Buy Lejendary Adventure</a> source books directly 
from this site, or visit <a href="http://www.rpgme.com/index.jsp?entry=lejendary" title="shop securely with your credit card">RPGme.com</a> 
to find all your gaming needs.</p>

<h4 style="margin:25px 0px 0px;;padding:0;">Latest News</h4>
<p><span class="date">07.06.2003</span> -- <span class="blurb">Dreamcadence Productions Introduces the &quot;Incredibook&quot;</span></p>
<p class="in">Dreamcadence Productions introduces a new format for upcoming adventure scenarios, Lejend Master tools, 
player aids, and more. <a href="template.php?page=ibook&amp;style=blaze" 
	title="download the Incredibook here">Download the new Incredibook&trade; demo</a> of the Lejends Magazine sample. Dreamcadence Productions is 
in negotiations with Hekaforge Productions and Total Reality Studios to possibly continue Lejends Magazine in the interactive, 
electronic Incredibook format. Dreamcadence Productions also announced the release of its first Lejendary Adventure scenario &quot;The Red 
Letter Day&quot; will be available in Incredibook format within a few weeks.
<h4 style="margin:25px 0px 0px;;padding:0;">Old News</h4>
<p><span class="date">03.31.2003</span> -- <span class="blurb">Gary Gygax Book Signing!</span></p>
<p class="in">Gary Gygax will be at the Higgins Armory Museum in
Worcester, MA on April 26th. As the only museum in the western hemisphere dedicated to the study of arms
and armor, the museum is excited to be hosting Gary Gygax, creator of
Dungeons &amp; Dragons, for a day-long seminar on Saturday, April 26, 2003.
Gary will also be conducting a public book-signing beginning at 2:00 p.m.
until 4:00 p.m. which is free with Museum admission. This is a rare
opportunity for gamers to meet the legend behind Dungeons &amp; Dragons, the
game that started it all!  Reservations are required for the workshop that
begins at 8:30 a.m. Pre-registration cost is $50 per person, lunch included.
Please contact Dianne Berg at dberg@higgins.org to register as space is
limited.  <a href="http://www.higgins.org" title="museum link">More Information</a></p>
<p><span class="date">03.26.2003</span> -- <span class="blurb">Lejendary Adventure Quick-Start Rules Now Available!</span></p>
<p class="in">The much anticipated Quick-Start Rules are now available exclusively from Lejendary.com! These rules contain everything 
needed to play the Lejendary Adventure game including example Avatars, and a mini-adventure. Learning to play Gary Gygax's Lejendary 
Adventure game has never been easier. <a href="template.php?page=misc&amp;style=blaze" 
	title="download the quick-start rules here">Check out</a> the Quick-Start Rules now!  </p>
<p><span class="date">12.11.2002</span> -- <span class="blurb">Lejendary.com Gets a New Look</span></p>
<p class="in">After several years of enduring the now famous Lejendary Lime theme, 
visitors to Lejendary.com finally get a new design. With the new 
<a href="http://www.webstandards.org" title="support web standards">standards compliant</a> 
implementation, users should experience faster page loads, an easier navigation interface, 
and a more appealing color scheme. For those who find it hard to say goodbye to the old classic 
lime theme, it's still available via the theme picker!  </p>
<p class="in">Along with the new design, there is much needed new content as well and more to follow soon. A few 
highlights of the new content are:</p>
<ul>
	<li>2 new product reviews plus links to 2 others</li>
	<li>1 new adventure scenario for download</li>
	<li>The Lejendary FAQ</li>
	<li>The errata</li>
</ul>
<p><span class="date">11.14.2002</span> -- <span class="blurb">Dreams Interactive Launches New LA Site</span></p>
<p class="in"> <a href="http://di.gamepoint.net/lejendary/en/index.php" title="dare to dream">Dreams Interactive</a> has launched their much anticipated web site for their 
upcoming <acronym title="Massively Multiplayer Online Role Playing Game">MMORPG</acronym> based on the Lejendary Adventure 
RPG rules, and set in the Lejendary Earth campaign setting. The new site features many screen 
shots of the first person perspective online RPG, news about the beta test, information on 
the game development, forums, and much more.</p>
<p><span class="date">11.01.2002</span> -- <span class="blurb">New Publisher of Lejendary Adventure Source Material</span></p>
<p class="in"> <a href="http://www.troll-lord.com" title="dare to dream">Troll Lord Games</a> recently published The Canting Crew and 
The Hermit both by Gary Gygax and both containing both d20 and Lejendary Adventure statistics and information. Troll Lord Games is the first 
game company to publish products with rules for the Lejendary Adventure system. The second will be <a href="http://www.fuzzyheroes.com">Inner City Game Designs</a> 
with the upcoming Castle Wolfmoon mega module that will also contain d20 and LA rules.</p>

<h4 style="margin:25px 0px 0px;padding:0;">Product Updates</h4>
<p><span class="date">Next Expected Product Release</span> -- <span class="blurb">Noble Knights and Dark Lands</span></p>
<p class="in"> The next official release from <a href="http://www.hekaforge.com" title="portal to mythic worlds">Hekaforge Productions</a> 
will be Noble Knights and Dark Lands. Noble Knights and Dark Lands is expected to be available in PDF format in late January, with the hard copy 
release scheduled for March.</p>
<p><span class="date">Latest Product Release</span> -- <span class="blurb">Chronicles of the Lejendary Earth Gazatteer</span></p>
<p class="in"> <a href="http://www.hekaforge.com" title="portal to mythic worlds">Hekaforge Productions</a> has released the long 
awaited first book in a series of source books detailing the Lejendary Earth campaign setting. The book is published in two editions 
the Standard Edition, and a very limited signed and numbered Author's Edition. The Author's Edition includes all the material in the 
Standard Edition plus a special parchment insert inside the front cover with Gary Gygax's signature. The Author's Edition also includes 
a CDROM with the book in electronic PDF format as well as all the maps in several different formats.</p>
